<devicesets>
<deviceset name="WE-HCFT_3521" urn="urn:adsk.eagle:component:14283564/7" prefix="L">
<description>WE-HCFT THT High Current Inductor
Shielded

Characteristics
Version to assure the mechanical stability
Magnetically shielded
Extremely low RDC

Ferrite (MnZn):
Inductance ranging from 1.5 µH up to 65 µH
Current capability up to 75 A (Saturation &gt;125 A)
Low core losses
Operating temperature -40 °C to +125 °C

Metal Alloy:
Inductance ranging from 0.6 µH up to 110 µH
Current capability up to 100 A (Saturation &gt;260 A)
Inductance stability across all operating temperatures
Operating temperature -55 °C to +155 °C

Applications
High current power supplies
Battery chargers
Solar inverter
Power factor correction circuits
Uninterruptible power supplies

Details see: www.we-online.com/en/components/products/WE-HCFT

Updated by Ella Wu 2024-11-19
2024 (C) Würth Elektronik</description>
